#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""prep — the prep run: businesses researched, built and drafted on Taylor's word (plan
~/projects/plans/28-prep-run.md, ROADMAP B64–B67). This file is born with B65, the research half:

  prep brief PLACE_ID [--json]      # the packet: the census row, the listing read with its reviews,
                                    # the reach row and its evidence, the presence link, the faults
  prep research PLACE_ID… [--parallel N] [--run ID] [--dry-run]
                                    # one Sonnet session a business, on the subscription login, in a
                                    # stamped directory whose settings deny Meta hosts and everything
                                    # outside it; keeps each session's log and usage, lints the facts
                                    # file, retries a failed lint once with the errors
  prep facts lint FILE [--listing listing.json] [--json]
                                    # every fact a source URL and its words; `high` only from the
                                    # listing, their own site, a public record or two independent
                                    # sources; never a review's words, a person's name, a price or a
                                    # street address in a publishable field
  prep doctor [--live]              # the login is the subscription (no API key), neither model is
                                    # Fable, the census and the Places key answer; --live pings both
                                    # models (one turn each) and the Places key (one read, $0.025)
  prep hook STAGE                   # internal: the PreToolUse hook the stamped settings run

B67, the run (the conductor: code conducts, Sonnet works, Opus judges):

  prep pick [--n 10] [--segment S] [--allow-calls] [--json]
                                    # n plus a reserve from the pool by fit: 10–300 reviews and 4.3★ or
                                    # better first, then a reach with evidence, then miles; three of a
                                    # category at most; minus the hold, the pipeline, the claimed, the
                                    # suppressed and anyone in a run still going. Spends nothing.
  prep run [--n 10] [--segment S] [--allow-calls] [--dry-run] [--no-publish] [--places ID…]
           [--reuse RUN] [--foreground]
                                    # doctor, pick, the marker requests/prep-<id>.running, the conductor
                                    # detached under `timeout`, one line back. --no-publish is the
                                    # rehearsal: everything but the publish, the hold and notify (the
                                    # outline goes to a file). --reuse copies a finished research run's
                                    # facts for the same place ids instead of researching them again.
  prep resume [ID] [--foreground]   # pick a stopped or killed run up where run.json says it was
  prep status [ID]                  # every business's stage, the usage by stage, the marker
  prep stop [ID]                    # stop the conductor and its sessions; resume carries on
  prep check [DIR] [--json] [--no-shot]
                                    # the seven gates (plan § Contracts) and the message's lint → check.json
  prep message [DIR] [--json]       # the channel, the link, the frame filled, the lint
  prep finish [ID] [--no-publish]   # the gates again, the publish (never --yes), the hold for the
                                    # delivered only, the ledger row, outline.md, notify
  prep publish [ID]                 # retry a failed publish, then the rest of finish
  prep last [ID] [--html]           # reprint the outline (or write it as one page)
  prep approve [--dry-run]          # Taylor's word on templates/prep/message.md (its hash)

The stages (plan § The shape): research (Sonnet, B65) → the facts gate (code) → build (Sonnet:
content.json and message.json, never HTML) → check (code) → judge (a fresh Opus session a round,
from the screenshots) → fix (the build session resumed with the list; two rounds, then dropped
and the next in the reserve takes the place) → batch (one Opus session over the night) → finish
(code). Four sessions at once (PREP_PARALLEL); a rate limit waits and retries; a stage that fails
twice drops that business. A model never publishes and never messages anyone.

Where things live (plan § Contracts): runs under PREP_STATE (~/.local/state/claude-tools/prep/)
as <date>-<letter>/ with run.json and one directory a business: listing.json (the listing read,
as on disk), packet.json (what `brief --json` prints), facts.json, log/research.stream.jsonl (the
session's whole stream: every tool call and its input), log/research.json (the session's result:
usage, cost at list, permission_denials, the model ids that ran), log/research.hook.jsonl (every
tool call the boundary saw and what it decided). Nothing a run writes is in a repo.

The boundary, three layers deep: `--restricted` (file tools confined to the directory, user and
project settings ignored), `--permission-mode dontAsk` with the stamped `.claude/settings.json`
(allow rules for the directory, web search and fetch; deny rules for Meta hosts and the log), and
that settings file's PreToolUse hook (`prep hook research`): refuses a Meta host, a path outside the
directory, any command but the lint, and the ninth search or the eleventh fetch, and logs each call.

Models: PREP_MODEL_BUILD (claude-sonnet-5-5) researches; PREP_MODEL_JUDGE (claude-opus-5-5) is
B67's. Every session names its model; a name with "fable" in it is refused, and a session whose
result shows a Fable model is failed. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and friends are stripped from the
session's environment, so it runs on Taylor's subscription login or not at all. PREP_CLAUDE
points at the `claude` to run (the tests' fake).

Money: the listing reads already on disk (`leads`' details cache) are used at any age; a place
with none costs one Places read (~$0.025, capped by PREP_PLACES_USD) and one ledger line.
Sessions on the subscription are notional (list price kept as `plan_usd_list`, never `cost_usd`).
"""

